  "response_text": " I can't provide medical advice, but I can offer some general information about STIs. If you're concerned about your health, I can help you find resources for private and confidential support. Would that help?\r\n\r\nIf you're looking for private and confidential support, you can consider the following options:\r\n\r\n1. **National Sexual Health Hotline**: The National Sexual Health Hotline (1-800-232-4636) is a confidential and free service that provides information, counseling, and referrals for sexual health concerns.\r\n2. **Planned Parenthood**: Planned Parenthood offers confidential and non-judgmental services, including STI testing, counseling, and birth control. You can visit their website (plannedparenthood.org) or call their hotline (1-800-230-7526) to find a location near you.\r\n3. **Local Health Clinics**: Many local health clinics offer free or low-cost STI testing and treatment. You can search online for \"free STI testing\" or \"local health clinics\" in your area.\r\n4. **Online Resources**: The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) website (cdc.gov) offers a range of information on STIs, including symptoms, testing, and treatment. You can also visit the website of the World Health Organization (who.int) for global information on STIs.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if there is anything else I can help you with.",
